WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.618
15 minutes of chaos

00:00:03.618 --> 00:00:05.661
that shook the world's biggest markets.

00:00:05.661 --> 00:00:08.289
What the heck is going on down here?

00:00:08.289 --> 00:00:09.123
I don't know.

00:00:09.123 --> 00:00:09.957
There is fear.

00:00:09.957 --> 00:00:11.626
This is capitulation really.

00:00:13.878 --> 00:00:17.632
On May 6th 2010, without warning,

00:00:17.632 --> 00:00:20.801
the U.S. stock market and
futures market just crushed.

00:00:20.801 --> 00:00:21.677
It can't be there.

00:00:21.677 --> 00:00:22.970
That is not a real price.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:23.596
The flash crash,

00:00:23.596 --> 00:00:25.890
which wiped a trillion
dollars off the value

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:28.100
of American companies in five minutes.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:29.977
To look at a price chart,

00:00:29.977 --> 00:00:32.230
it looked like a kind of runaway elevator.

00:00:33.773 --> 00:00:35.233
It took authorities

00:00:35.233 --> 00:00:38.653
five years guys to track
down this lone British trader

00:00:38.653 --> 00:00:40.947
allegedly involved in a 2010 flash crash.

00:00:40.947 --> 00:00:41.864
Navinder Singh Sarao,

00:00:41.864 --> 00:00:43.658
dubbed the hound of Hounslow

00:00:43.658 --> 00:00:45.993
has been accused of
manipulating the market.

00:00:45.993 --> 00:00:49.121
U.S. regulators claim he
made about $40 Million.

00:00:51.582 --> 00:00:53.417
So Navinder Sarao

00:00:53.417 --> 00:00:57.171
he seems to be for all
intents and purposes,

00:00:57.171 --> 00:01:00.508
like a sort of arch criminal mastermind.

00:01:00.508 --> 00:01:02.134
What they find is very different.

00:01:03.803 --> 00:01:05.888
We're in a working class neighborhood

00:01:05.888 --> 00:01:08.266
about 11 miles from the city center

00:01:08.266 --> 00:01:09.642
and the financial district.

00:01:10.977 --> 00:01:13.354
It was hard to believe

00:01:13.354 --> 00:01:18.359
somebody trading this size
was just a lone trader.

00:01:18.359 --> 00:01:21.070
But that's where we were.

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:23.990
I think it's ridiculous
to say that this guy

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:26.450
in this house in the
suburbs, in England caused-

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:27.285
Took down the market?

00:01:27.285 --> 00:01:28.327
It's ridiculous.

00:01:28.327 --> 00:01:30.496
If he really did, as the
U.S. prosecutors alleged

00:01:30.496 --> 00:01:32.415
make 40 million bucks,

00:01:32.415 --> 00:01:33.499
three people have now said to me,

00:01:33.499 --> 00:01:37.044
"Well, then why the heck is he
still living on our street?"

00:01:37.044 --> 00:01:38.838
On the one hand,

00:01:38.838 --> 00:01:40.339
he was a kind of common cheat.

00:01:40.339 --> 00:01:44.010
He purposefully manipulated the markets.

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:45.136
On the other hand,

00:01:45.136 --> 00:01:46.512
he's this kind of genius kid

00:01:46.512 --> 00:01:47.888
from the wrong side of the tracks,

00:01:47.888 --> 00:01:50.599
who just decided to almost
stick two fingers up

00:01:50.599 --> 00:01:52.852
at the man and the establishment.

00:01:52.852 --> 00:01:54.645
And I think everyone could kind of relate

00:01:54.645 --> 00:01:56.063
to wanting to do that.

00:02:05.114 --> 00:02:06.115
I'm Liam Vaughan.

00:02:06.115 --> 00:02:09.160
I'm an investigative journalist
with Bloomberg in London,

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:12.455
and I'm the author of a
book called, "Flash Crash",

00:02:12.455 --> 00:02:16.542
which tells the story
of the 2010 flash crash.

00:02:16.542 --> 00:02:18.878
And Navinder Singh Sarao

00:02:18.878 --> 00:02:20.129
the British day trader

00:02:20.129 --> 00:02:21.756
who was accused by the U.S. government

00:02:21.756 --> 00:02:23.341
of causing it from his bedroom.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:33.351
So Navinder Sarao was in a lot of ways

00:02:33.351 --> 00:02:37.021
quite an ordinary kid from
a working class neighborhood

00:02:37.021 --> 00:02:39.148
underneath the Heathrow flight path.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.153
Had a bit of a gob on him

00:02:44.153 --> 00:02:46.614
was always very kind of
fast and quick-witted,

00:02:46.614 --> 00:02:49.492
but also a little bit
quick to kind of anger.

00:02:49.492 --> 00:02:51.619
He had this gift for multiplication

00:02:51.619 --> 00:02:54.455
and for rapid thinking and for arithmetic.

00:02:54.455 --> 00:02:56.040
After university,

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.126
he opens a newspaper and
it's the Evening Standard

00:02:59.126 --> 00:03:02.421
and there's an advert in there which says

00:03:02.421 --> 00:03:05.174
"Wanted, Futures Traders.

00:03:05.174 --> 00:03:07.176
"Must work well under pressure."

00:03:07.176 --> 00:03:08.135
Which, as you can imagine

00:03:08.135 --> 00:03:12.098
is not how they typically
recruit staff at JP Morgan.

00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:19.146
But this was a job at
these kind of fledgling

00:03:19.146 --> 00:03:21.607
entities that were known as arcades

00:03:21.607 --> 00:03:22.733
at that point in time.

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:25.903
All the learning takes
place on the trading floor

00:03:25.903 --> 00:03:28.197
among some of the best traders in Europe.

00:03:28.197 --> 00:03:31.033
Essentially you eat what you kill.

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:32.535
And that's something really powerful

00:03:32.535 --> 00:03:34.161
when you're seeking a career

00:03:34.161 --> 00:03:36.288
where you make your decisions

00:03:36.288 --> 00:03:38.874
and profit on those on
decisions on a daily basis.

00:03:42.837 --> 00:03:46.507
So Futex is above Waitrose Supermarket.

00:03:46.507 --> 00:03:50.302
It's about 45 minutes outside
of the City of London,

00:03:50.302 --> 00:03:53.305
miles away from the
skyscrapers of the City

00:03:53.305 --> 00:03:55.224
and Canary Wharf.

00:03:55.224 --> 00:04:00.020
And at first it's a fairly shabby office,

00:04:00.896 --> 00:04:02.022
which has got connections

00:04:02.022 --> 00:04:04.442
to the world's commodities exchanges.

00:04:05.526 --> 00:04:08.237
Now Nav had this kind of
background in computer games.

00:04:08.237 --> 00:04:11.031
He was incredibly focused and gifted at

00:04:11.031 --> 00:04:12.950
games like Halo and FIFA.

00:04:13.826 --> 00:04:15.453
And he was able to, he found

00:04:15.453 --> 00:04:17.872
sit for hours and hours at a time

00:04:17.872 --> 00:04:21.083
just focusing on one task
until he'd mastered it.

00:04:25.379 --> 00:04:28.757
Fast forward a couple
of years and Navinder

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:34.638
is almost like a kind of
enigmatic figure at Futex.

00:04:34.638 --> 00:04:38.184
He has decided that he
can't stand the disruption

00:04:38.184 --> 00:04:41.061
of his colleagues chatting
amongst themselves,

00:04:41.061 --> 00:04:42.980
getting very excited with market moves.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:45.900
So he moves himself to a desk,

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:47.401
completely isolated,

00:04:47.401 --> 00:04:49.487
where he can work on his own.

00:04:49.487 --> 00:04:51.572
He buys himself a pair of ear defenders.

00:04:51.572 --> 00:04:52.531
They're not headphones,

00:04:52.531 --> 00:04:53.949
they're literally ear defenders

00:04:53.949 --> 00:04:55.534
of the type that road workers use.

00:04:57.661 --> 00:04:58.829
So to the other traders there,

00:04:58.829 --> 00:05:01.373
lots of them wannabe traders

00:05:01.373 --> 00:05:02.958
he was almost like a god-like figure.

00:05:02.958 --> 00:05:05.503
Because they would see how
much money he was making

00:05:05.503 --> 00:05:07.838
the size of the trades
that he was placing.

00:05:07.838 --> 00:05:09.757
And it was just a
complete mystery to them

00:05:09.757 --> 00:05:11.050
how he was able to do it.

00:05:14.637 --> 00:05:17.556
So Nav traded a financial
instrument called the E-mini,

00:05:17.556 --> 00:05:19.934
which essentially tracks the S&amp;P 500,

00:05:19.934 --> 00:05:23.812
which is a barometer essentially
of the US stock market.

00:05:23.812 --> 00:05:25.940
And he's able to

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:29.318
build a sense, based on his
constant reading of the market,

00:05:29.318 --> 00:05:31.612
and he's almost kind of

00:05:32.571 --> 00:05:35.574
preternatural ability to determine

00:05:35.574 --> 00:05:38.202
whether he thinks the market
is about to go up or down

00:05:38.202 --> 00:05:39.787
based on what's happening

00:05:39.787 --> 00:05:41.956
and the orders that are
entering and leaving the market.

00:05:46.377 --> 00:05:49.880
Nav leaves Feutex in 2008

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:52.550
in the midst of the
global financial crisis.

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:54.969
The banking sector bore
the brunt of the collapse

00:05:54.969 --> 00:05:57.096
with shares in Europe's major banks

00:05:57.096 --> 00:05:59.890
tanking by as much as 9%.

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:02.643
By that stage, he's in his late 20s

00:06:02.643 --> 00:06:05.854
and he's already accumulated
about $2 million.

00:06:05.854 --> 00:06:07.690
Lehman Brothers has just collapsed.

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:09.692
I don't think anyone really expected

00:06:09.692 --> 00:06:11.610
a bank as big as Lehman to

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:13.153
be in a position that it's in now.

00:06:13.153 --> 00:06:16.574
The entire global financial
system is in danger.

00:06:17.866 --> 00:06:21.287
We're in the midst of a
serious financial crisis

00:06:21.287 --> 00:06:22.955
and the Federal Government is responding

00:06:22.955 --> 00:06:24.582
with decisive action.

00:06:24.582 --> 00:06:25.833
There's governments around the world

00:06:25.833 --> 00:06:28.168
stepping into save financial institutions.

00:06:28.168 --> 00:06:30.754
And this is Nav's, I guess,

00:06:30.754 --> 00:06:33.632
first very big and successful trade,

00:06:33.632 --> 00:06:35.426
almost career-defining trade.

00:06:35.426 --> 00:06:39.430
He decides that with market
prices as low as they are,

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:41.140
eventually the government
is gonna have to step in

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:42.016
and rescue them.

00:06:42.016 --> 00:06:44.059
So he places all of his money,

00:06:44.059 --> 00:06:46.770
which at that stage is a
couple of million dollars

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:48.981
on this bet that the
government is gonna intervene

00:06:48.981 --> 00:06:51.275
and prices will rise again.

00:06:51.275 --> 00:06:54.153
And he times it absolutely perfectly.

00:06:54.153 --> 00:06:55.487
He places a trade on a Friday.

00:06:55.487 --> 00:06:56.322
The following Monday,

00:06:56.322 --> 00:06:58.699
the U.S. government
announces this big bazooka.

00:06:58.699 --> 00:06:59.658
Under our proposal,

00:06:59.658 --> 00:07:02.369
the Federal Government
would put up to 700 billion

00:07:02.369 --> 00:07:04.413
taxpayer dollars on the line

00:07:04.413 --> 00:07:05.748
to purchase troubled assets

00:07:05.748 --> 00:07:08.167
that are clogging the financial system.

00:07:08.167 --> 00:07:09.877
And over the course of that week

00:07:11.128 --> 00:07:14.048
U.S. prices increased by 19%.

00:07:14.048 --> 00:07:16.759
Nav had ridden the wave, the entire wave,

00:07:16.759 --> 00:07:19.678
and he goes from a position of $2 million

00:07:19.678 --> 00:07:21.972
to suddenly being worth $15 million.

00:07:21.972 --> 00:07:23.849
And really that's when
he hits the big time.

00:07:38.697 --> 00:07:40.491
One of the striking things about Navinder,

00:07:40.491 --> 00:07:42.785
is that he really doesn't spend

00:07:42.785 --> 00:07:44.662
any of the money he makes at all.

00:07:44.662 --> 00:07:46.246
He kinda makes a decision early on

00:07:46.246 --> 00:07:48.040
that he doesn't wanna tell
his friends and family

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.208
about the money.

00:07:49.208 --> 00:07:51.877
He doesn't want to be seen as a show off,

00:07:51.877 --> 00:07:54.546
and he doesn't want them
to treat him differently.

00:07:54.546 --> 00:07:56.215
So rather than actually spending the money

00:07:56.215 --> 00:07:57.925
or telling other people about it

00:07:57.925 --> 00:07:58.926
he just keeps it to himself.

00:07:58.926 --> 00:08:03.430
And he lets the dollars grow
in his profit and loss account.

00:08:15.067 --> 00:08:18.570
You would have thought
that Nav will be delighted

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:20.197
at the money that he's made

00:08:20.197 --> 00:08:22.116
and his position and how successful he is

00:08:22.116 --> 00:08:25.536
but there's something that's
frustrating and bugging him.

00:08:25.536 --> 00:08:27.871
And that is the arrival in the markets

00:08:27.871 --> 00:08:30.040
of this kind of new breed of participant

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:32.710
that are known as high frequency traders.

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:35.629
So what is high frequency trading?

00:08:35.629 --> 00:08:36.797
Well, high frequency trading

00:08:36.797 --> 00:08:39.633
is where the markets have evolved to.

00:08:39.633 --> 00:08:42.720
So people have written rules
that would normally be executed

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:45.597
in a human being's
brain into the computer.

00:08:45.597 --> 00:08:49.893
And they trade at very high
frequencies and high speeds

00:08:49.893 --> 00:08:52.020
because the computers and
the communications lines

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:53.188
allow them to.

00:08:53.188 --> 00:08:56.275
They buy just before other people do

00:08:56.275 --> 00:08:58.861
and then resell them at a small increase

00:08:58.861 --> 00:09:00.529
pocketing the tiny profit.

00:09:00.529 --> 00:09:03.741
So what's happening is a kind of skim.

00:09:03.741 --> 00:09:05.868
People are getting
scalped in the market.

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:08.036
Well, for Nav

00:09:08.036 --> 00:09:09.788
he wasn't so interested in the kind of

00:09:09.788 --> 00:09:11.248
equality of the markets.

00:09:11.248 --> 00:09:13.333
He was more frustrated that his profits

00:09:13.333 --> 00:09:15.794
and his ability to kind of make money

00:09:15.794 --> 00:09:19.798
was getting squashed by these robots.

00:09:19.798 --> 00:09:23.594
We have executed 21
million shares already.

00:09:23.594 --> 00:09:27.306
Wow and we are not even three minutes in.

00:09:28.307 --> 00:09:31.977
So in 2009, 2010,

00:09:31.977 --> 00:09:34.146
he makes this kind of fateful decision

00:09:34.146 --> 00:09:36.899
that he's gonna build his own robot

00:09:36.899 --> 00:09:39.985
that's gonna fight back
against the HFT firms,

00:09:39.985 --> 00:09:40.819
and what he was planning to do

00:09:40.819 --> 00:09:42.821
was to essentially manipulate the market.

00:09:44.406 --> 00:09:48.285
And after a few, I
guess, teething problems,

00:09:48.285 --> 00:09:51.330
it starts to work incredibly well.

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:52.706
From his bedroom,

00:09:52.706 --> 00:09:55.876
he's able to routinely nudge the world's

00:09:55.876 --> 00:09:57.586
second largest Futures market.

00:09:57.586 --> 00:10:02.591
He could quite easily make half
a million dollars in a day.

00:10:03.217 --> 00:10:05.052
In the week before the flash crash,

00:10:05.052 --> 00:10:07.554
on one day he made $400,000.

00:10:07.554 --> 00:10:10.140
The next day he made $800,000.

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:12.142
And if you can imagine
he lives in Hounslow,

00:10:12.142 --> 00:10:15.896
his parent's house is worth $300,000

00:10:15.896 --> 00:10:18.857
and he's making three times
that amount every single day.

00:10:24.571 --> 00:10:26.865
Welcome to Street Signs on
this Thursday afternoon,

00:10:26.865 --> 00:10:28.742
a big afternoon as stocks accelerate

00:10:28.742 --> 00:10:29.576
their slide.

00:10:29.576 --> 00:10:32.913
May 6, 2010 is an extremely volatile day.

00:10:32.913 --> 00:10:35.791
There is a feeling that
the European Central Bank

00:10:35.791 --> 00:10:39.628
and bankers have lost
control of this situation.

00:10:39.628 --> 00:10:42.089
There's this index known as the 'fear index'

00:10:42.089 --> 00:10:43.757
in financial markets,

00:10:43.757 --> 00:10:47.344
which kind of monitors volatility.

00:10:47.344 --> 00:10:50.305
And that morning it was up 30%

00:10:50.305 --> 00:10:53.934
and Navinder starts to use his machines

00:10:53.934 --> 00:10:57.396
to pump sell orders
into an already falling

00:10:57.396 --> 00:10:59.022
and a very, very volatile market.

00:11:01.608 --> 00:11:03.193
For Nav, you know,

00:11:03.193 --> 00:11:05.946
if you can imagine a big wave surfer

00:11:05.946 --> 00:11:07.447
and he looks out at the swell

00:11:07.447 --> 00:11:09.283
and there's just huge waves.

00:11:09.283 --> 00:11:10.284
It's like the dream.

00:11:10.284 --> 00:11:14.371
It's like a once in a year long condition.

00:11:14.371 --> 00:11:15.706
He switches his computer on

00:11:15.706 --> 00:11:17.332
at half past nine in the morning,

00:11:17.332 --> 00:11:19.459
and he starts pumping these sell orders

00:11:19.459 --> 00:11:21.628
using his algorithm into the market.

00:11:23.005 --> 00:11:24.214
In the afternoon

00:11:24.214 --> 00:11:26.550
he gets to a point where he's placing

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:28.927
$200 million of orders,

00:11:28.927 --> 00:11:31.430
and he's having this huge success.

00:11:32.598 --> 00:11:35.142
At 1:40 PM, exactly,

00:11:35.142 --> 00:11:36.977
it's not clear exactly why,

00:11:36.977 --> 00:11:39.605
maybe his mom had called
him down for dinner,

00:11:39.605 --> 00:11:41.148
it's seven o'clock in London,

00:11:41.148 --> 00:11:43.650
Nav decides to switch the computer off.

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:44.568
Great day's work.

00:11:44.568 --> 00:11:47.404
He's made $950,000.

00:11:50.157 --> 00:11:51.283
Completely wiped out.

00:11:51.283 --> 00:11:54.077
Now exactly one minute after that

00:11:54.077 --> 00:11:57.831
is when the market starts
falling at a rate and a velocity

00:11:57.831 --> 00:11:58.832
that it never has before.

00:11:58.832 --> 00:12:00.918
Traders say this is the craziest day

00:12:00.918 --> 00:12:01.835
they have ever seen.

00:12:01.835 --> 00:12:04.713
Nav is essentially a bystander

00:12:04.713 --> 00:12:06.840
as the bottom falls out of the market.

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:09.885
And we have this, you
know, very dramatic event

00:12:09.885 --> 00:12:12.179
which comes to be known
as the flash crash.

00:12:12.179 --> 00:12:13.055
The flash crash,

00:12:13.055 --> 00:12:14.723
which wiped a trillion dollars

00:12:14.723 --> 00:12:17.809
off the value of American
companies in five minutes.

00:12:17.809 --> 00:12:20.062
The biggest sudden fall on record

00:12:20.062 --> 00:12:22.105
before markets bounced right back.

00:12:22.105 --> 00:12:23.398
Officials are meeting this week

00:12:23.398 --> 00:12:26.860
with executives from the New
York Stock Exchange and NASDAQ

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:29.237
to see if the issue of
different exchanges

00:12:29.237 --> 00:12:30.614
having different rules

00:12:30.614 --> 00:12:33.742
played a role in
Thursday's rapid free fall.

00:12:33.742 --> 00:12:35.577
Over the next couple of months

00:12:35.577 --> 00:12:37.704
there is a very deep dive

00:12:37.704 --> 00:12:41.124
into exactly what was going on that day,

00:12:41.124 --> 00:12:42.876
who was trading,

00:12:42.876 --> 00:12:44.711
and trying to get to the bottom of this

00:12:44.711 --> 00:12:47.756
really what was a mystery
at that point in time.

00:12:47.756 --> 00:12:50.842
The U.S. regulators a few months later

00:12:50.842 --> 00:12:53.387
produced this very detailed report

00:12:53.387 --> 00:12:56.306
in which they discuss what happened.

00:12:56.306 --> 00:12:58.517
No where to be seen in
this hundred page report

00:12:58.517 --> 00:13:00.435
was any reference to manipulation

00:13:00.435 --> 00:13:01.645
and certainly no reference

00:13:01.645 --> 00:13:03.730
to a guy in his bedroom in Hounslow.

00:13:07.401 --> 00:13:09.069
So Navinder, as you can imagine,

00:13:09.069 --> 00:13:11.947
is completely oblivious to
these investigations in the U.S.,

00:13:11.947 --> 00:13:15.534
and you know, he only becomes
more and more successful

00:13:15.534 --> 00:13:16.618
after the flash crash.

00:13:17.577 --> 00:13:18.745
At this point in time,

00:13:18.745 --> 00:13:20.914
you start to have the exchange

00:13:20.914 --> 00:13:23.041
and the regulators almost noticing

00:13:23.041 --> 00:13:24.459
that he's canceling a lot of orders,

00:13:24.459 --> 00:13:26.628
and famously at one point in time

00:13:26.628 --> 00:13:30.340
he gets a letter from the exchange

00:13:30.340 --> 00:13:32.759
asking him to essentially
explain what he's been up to

00:13:32.759 --> 00:13:33.593
and he tells them

00:13:33.593 --> 00:13:34.594
"To kiss my ass".

00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:38.807
Ultimately, it wouldn't be the regulators

00:13:38.807 --> 00:13:39.808
that would catch Nav.

00:13:39.808 --> 00:13:41.893
It will be someone more like him,

00:13:41.893 --> 00:13:43.562
another day trader

00:13:43.562 --> 00:13:45.355
who was operating,

00:13:45.355 --> 00:13:46.356
not out of his bedroom,

00:13:46.356 --> 00:13:48.942
but in a small firm in Chicago,

00:13:48.942 --> 00:13:52.279
who was back testing his own software

00:13:52.279 --> 00:13:55.157
and happened to notice that
on the day of the flash crash

00:13:55.157 --> 00:13:57.617
there were all these
weird blocks of orders

00:13:57.617 --> 00:13:59.536
that were entering and
then leaving the market.

00:13:59.536 --> 00:14:01.705
And he blows the whistle

00:14:01.705 --> 00:14:05.000
and the information arrives at the CFTC.

00:14:06.543 --> 00:14:08.712
The CFTC at that point in time

00:14:08.712 --> 00:14:11.715
has spent years really being a regulator

00:14:11.715 --> 00:14:13.508
for agricultural markets.

00:14:13.508 --> 00:14:15.969
To understand and to be able to analyze

00:14:15.969 --> 00:14:18.096
what's going on in financial markets

00:14:18.096 --> 00:14:22.476
at a kind of granular level
is incredibly complicated.

00:14:22.476 --> 00:14:24.394
And at that point in time,

00:14:24.394 --> 00:14:26.313
there's only a few people at the CFTC

00:14:26.313 --> 00:14:27.856
who've got that expertise,

00:14:27.856 --> 00:14:29.816
one of them is Jessica Harris.

00:14:29.816 --> 00:14:32.319
Can I get like an
emissary, like a stand in?

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:34.404
No?

00:14:34.404 --> 00:14:38.533
The data sets that we
reviewed for Nav's activity

00:14:38.533 --> 00:14:42.370
showed he would place
these orders together

00:14:42.370 --> 00:14:44.623
and modify those orders several,

00:14:44.623 --> 00:14:46.208
sometimes thousands of times,

00:14:46.208 --> 00:14:48.168
or hundreds of times before

00:14:48.168 --> 00:14:51.880
then canceling them and not getting hit.

00:14:52.714 --> 00:14:54.674
So effectively, U.S. prosecutors
say that Navinder Sarao

00:14:54.674 --> 00:14:56.676
was engaged in illegal trading.

00:14:56.676 --> 00:14:58.470
They say that he was doing

00:14:58.470 --> 00:15:00.263
something called spoof and layering.

00:15:00.263 --> 00:15:03.600
Basically, traders will flood the market

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:05.102
with the intention of then -

00:15:05.102 --> 00:15:07.354
with orders of a certain security,

00:15:07.354 --> 00:15:09.856
with the intention of then
canceling those orders.

00:15:09.856 --> 00:15:12.484
And what that does is it artificially

00:15:12.484 --> 00:15:15.237
drives the price of that
security up or down.

00:15:16.154 --> 00:15:17.614
So after a year or so,

00:15:17.614 --> 00:15:20.117
the CFTC starts to become comfortable

00:15:20.117 --> 00:15:23.537
that they've identified
genuine manipulation

00:15:23.537 --> 00:15:25.539
and massive scale manipulation.

00:15:25.539 --> 00:15:27.124
And so what they do at that point

00:15:27.124 --> 00:15:30.794
is they decide to get involved
the Department of Justice.

00:15:30.794 --> 00:15:33.296
They're the ones that
can throw you in jail.

00:15:33.296 --> 00:15:35.423
They're the ones that can subpoena you.

00:15:35.423 --> 00:15:36.925
They're the ones that
you really don't want

00:15:36.925 --> 00:15:38.552
knocking on your door.

00:15:38.552 --> 00:15:41.179
So in February of 2015,

00:15:41.179 --> 00:15:45.183
a judge signs an arrest warrant for Nav.

00:15:45.183 --> 00:15:47.477
And at that point essentially
his fate is sealed

00:15:47.477 --> 00:15:48.812
he just doesn't know it yet.

00:16:04.119 --> 00:16:06.037
So it's the morning of the arrest

00:16:06.037 --> 00:16:09.416
and half a dozen police officers,

00:16:09.416 --> 00:16:13.128
two prosecutors from the
U.S. Justice Department

00:16:13.128 --> 00:16:16.423
and two agents from the FBI

00:16:16.423 --> 00:16:21.428
rendezvous at a McDonald's
that Nav knows incredibly well,

00:16:21.428 --> 00:16:23.513
which is about a mile from his house.

00:16:23.513 --> 00:16:26.600
And they discuss how they're gonna arrest

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:28.185
this criminal mastermind.

00:16:31.813 --> 00:16:33.940
As the sun rises that morning,

00:16:33.940 --> 00:16:36.693
they creeped through
the streets of Hounslow

00:16:36.693 --> 00:16:38.445
and arrive at this address,

00:16:40.447 --> 00:16:43.575
where sleeping upstairs
in bed is Navinder.

00:16:45.452 --> 00:16:49.164
They knock on the door
and Nav's dad answers.

00:16:49.164 --> 00:16:50.540
He shouts upstairs

00:16:51.458 --> 00:16:54.753
and down the stairs, kind of pads,

00:16:54.753 --> 00:16:58.173
this guy in tracksuit
bottoms and a t-shirt,

00:16:58.173 --> 00:17:00.300
his hair askew,

00:17:00.300 --> 00:17:02.052
looking utterly confused.

00:17:03.511 --> 00:17:06.348
As he's led out of the house in handcuffs,

00:17:06.348 --> 00:17:07.766
he turns to one of the officers

00:17:07.766 --> 00:17:10.936
and says, "Can I run
upstairs a minute bruv

00:17:11.811 --> 00:17:14.814
there's a football match on
telly that I want to record."

00:17:14.814 --> 00:17:15.649
And the officer says,

00:17:15.649 --> 00:17:16.858
"I don't think you're gonna get a chance

00:17:16.858 --> 00:17:19.319
to watch that for a while son."

00:17:19.319 --> 00:17:20.195
You know, as it turned out,

00:17:20.195 --> 00:17:23.615
he wouldn't set foot in the
house for another four months.

00:17:23.615 --> 00:17:25.492
Pretty hard for people
in this neighborhood

00:17:25.492 --> 00:17:26.368
to get their heads around.

00:17:26.368 --> 00:17:28.620
This is a real working class neighborhood.

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:29.704
Excuse me sir,

00:17:29.704 --> 00:17:31.706
is the family making any comments today?

00:17:32.958 --> 00:17:34.042
I'm very surprised.

00:17:34.042 --> 00:17:35.168
You know what I mean?

00:17:35.168 --> 00:17:36.503
I've lived here all my life,

00:17:36.503 --> 00:17:39.130
and I know a lot of the
neighbors around there.

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:40.674
Everyone gets on, you know.

00:17:40.674 --> 00:17:41.508
Very, very nice

00:17:42.550 --> 00:17:44.761
His dad is probably not feeling well

00:17:44.761 --> 00:17:46.304
from quite a long time, so.

00:17:46.304 --> 00:17:47.764
So a lot of people in the markets

00:17:47.764 --> 00:17:48.974
and particularly people like him

00:17:48.974 --> 00:17:50.517
that were on the outskirts,

00:17:50.517 --> 00:17:52.435
that were day traders,

00:17:52.435 --> 00:17:55.272
they almost idolized this guy

00:17:55.272 --> 00:17:57.899
who had made a fortune from nothing

00:17:57.899 --> 00:17:59.609
and had found a way to fight back

00:17:59.609 --> 00:18:02.737
against a system in which, you know,

00:18:02.737 --> 00:18:06.241
the most well-funded
and well-connected firms

00:18:06.241 --> 00:18:07.659
are the most successful.

00:18:07.659 --> 00:18:09.911
And for guys like, you
know, for guys like them,

00:18:09.911 --> 00:18:12.664
it was almost impossible to be profitable.

00:18:12.664 --> 00:18:14.708
Ryan Chilcote sat down with a former boss

00:18:14.708 --> 00:18:17.544
of the alleged flash crash
trader, Navinder Sarao.

00:18:19.004 --> 00:18:21.172
It can go one of two ways.

00:18:21.172 --> 00:18:26.177
If he's found innocence
of the allegations,

00:18:26.886 --> 00:18:31.891
then he will be the
world's superstar trader.

00:18:32.142 --> 00:18:33.727
The British trader accused of helping

00:18:33.727 --> 00:18:36.062
cause the May 2010 flash crash

00:18:36.062 --> 00:18:38.565
spent last night in jail.

00:18:38.565 --> 00:18:39.649
They threw the book at him.

00:18:39.649 --> 00:18:42.277
There was 22 criminal counts against him,

00:18:42.277 --> 00:18:47.032
which had a cumulative total
of 380 years in prison.

00:18:47.032 --> 00:18:50.410
And the judge looks at
how much money he's made

00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:53.621
and sets bail at 5 million pounds.

00:18:53.621 --> 00:18:55.415
And, you know, for Nav,

00:18:55.415 --> 00:18:57.083
who's worth tens of millions of pounds,

00:18:57.083 --> 00:18:59.169
that should be fairly easy to get hold of.

00:18:59.169 --> 00:19:01.796
What's unclear to me is
how much money he made.

00:19:01.796 --> 00:19:02.756
And such a great trader,

00:19:02.756 --> 00:19:04.966
I'm assuming he probably
has seven and a half million

00:19:04.966 --> 00:19:06.092
just lying around.

00:19:06.092 --> 00:19:06.926
Yeah.

00:19:06.926 --> 00:19:08.303
So everybody's asking that question

00:19:08.303 --> 00:19:10.472
because he was granted
the conditional bail,

00:19:10.472 --> 00:19:12.265
but he has failed to post

00:19:12.265 --> 00:19:13.600
the seven and a half million dollars.

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:15.310
So now he's still in the clink.

00:19:15.310 --> 00:19:17.020
His lawyers start getting in touch

00:19:17.020 --> 00:19:18.938
with his various investment advisors

00:19:18.938 --> 00:19:20.774
who taken Nav's money over the years

00:19:20.774 --> 00:19:24.069
and suddenly they don't answer his calls

00:19:24.069 --> 00:19:25.445
and it becomes clear,

00:19:26.446 --> 00:19:28.531
disturbingly over time,

00:19:28.531 --> 00:19:30.617
that all the money that Nav's put aside,

00:19:30.617 --> 00:19:31.743
all the profits that he's made

00:19:31.743 --> 00:19:33.912
over his successful trading career,

00:19:35.121 --> 00:19:37.707
may not be safe after all.

00:19:37.707 --> 00:19:39.751
Has he been scammed out of $50 million?

00:19:40.627 --> 00:19:42.796
It looks that way Mark, yes.

00:19:42.796 --> 00:19:43.797
I mean, it's one of those stories

00:19:43.797 --> 00:19:47.050
that it's almost a too crazy to believe.

00:19:47.050 --> 00:19:51.554
Any anyone that offered
him a good rate of return.

00:19:51.554 --> 00:19:53.848
Some of the places that he put his money

00:19:53.848 --> 00:19:55.642
offered him risk-free returns.

00:19:55.642 --> 00:19:58.269
And he seems to have
been kind of willingly,

00:19:58.269 --> 00:20:01.147
you know, very kind of
willing to put it there.

00:20:01.147 --> 00:20:02.857
Nav on the one hand

00:20:02.857 --> 00:20:04.943
is this kind of brilliant,
brilliant trader,

00:20:04.943 --> 00:20:07.487
on the other he's a kind of naive kid

00:20:07.487 --> 00:20:08.863
who's never worked at a bank,

00:20:08.863 --> 00:20:10.657
has no commercial experience.

00:20:10.657 --> 00:20:13.201
And, you know, for want of a better word

00:20:13.201 --> 00:20:15.412
has been duped by these guys.

00:20:15.412 --> 00:20:16.913
The bulk of his money

00:20:16.913 --> 00:20:19.999
was with this entrepreneurial called Jesus

00:20:19.999 --> 00:20:22.502
who turned around and said,

00:20:22.502 --> 00:20:24.587
"Mea culpa, I lost it all.

00:20:24.587 --> 00:20:26.297
You know, I'll give it
back to you when I can."

00:20:26.297 --> 00:20:29.759
And in the end, the judge
decides to lower bail.

00:20:29.759 --> 00:20:32.011
So his parents have to put
up the value of their house

00:20:32.011 --> 00:20:33.388
and he gets let out.

00:20:33.388 --> 00:20:34.889
The British trader accused

00:20:34.889 --> 00:20:38.143
of helping cause the May 2010 flash crash

00:20:38.143 --> 00:20:41.855
is free on seven and a
half million dollars bail.

00:20:41.855 --> 00:20:43.398
The judge in the U.K. decided

00:20:43.398 --> 00:20:46.609
that he should be extradited to the U.S.

00:20:46.609 --> 00:20:48.236
to stand trial.

00:20:48.236 --> 00:20:50.738
And what happens next is that his lawyer,

00:20:50.738 --> 00:20:52.824
who used to work at the
Department of Justice himself

00:20:52.824 --> 00:20:54.409
as a prosecutor,

00:20:54.409 --> 00:20:58.997
flies to Washington and
tries to strike a deal.

00:20:58.997 --> 00:21:01.291
And he speaks to the prosecutors

00:21:01.291 --> 00:21:03.793
and he says, "Yes, you could go to trial,

00:21:03.793 --> 00:21:05.545
but there's a risk that you could lose.

00:21:05.545 --> 00:21:07.046
And Navinder is a very vulnerable guy.

00:21:07.046 --> 00:21:09.424
Maybe the jury would feel sorry for him.

00:21:09.424 --> 00:21:10.717
Why don't we strike a deal?"

00:21:10.717 --> 00:21:14.137
You know, we saw this guy who, you know,

00:21:14.137 --> 00:21:17.724
initially, we believed to
be part of a bank or an HFT

00:21:17.724 --> 00:21:19.142
based on his tradings activity

00:21:19.142 --> 00:21:21.436
and the size and the
money that he was making

00:21:21.436 --> 00:21:23.938
to somebody who evolved

00:21:23.938 --> 00:21:26.524
into just, you know, a lone trader

00:21:26.524 --> 00:21:28.902
or an individual trading out of his house

00:21:28.902 --> 00:21:31.154
who didn't spend any money.

00:21:31.154 --> 00:21:32.405
And it was, I think,

00:21:33.740 --> 00:21:38.328
difficult to see what
that motive was for him.

00:21:38.328 --> 00:21:40.288
I'd say the DOJ, you know,

00:21:40.288 --> 00:21:42.582
weighs it up and
ultimately agrees to that.

00:21:42.582 --> 00:21:44.125
And then he pleads guilty.

00:21:44.125 --> 00:21:46.836
By the time it came to
Nav being sentenced

00:21:46.836 --> 00:21:50.423
you have the U.S. authorities

00:21:50.423 --> 00:21:52.425
having a very different perception of him.

00:21:52.425 --> 00:21:54.761
On the one hand, he
was incredibly helpful.

00:21:54.761 --> 00:21:57.847
He opened their eyes to
how market abuse goes on.

00:21:57.847 --> 00:21:59.933
He helped them build a number of cases.

00:21:59.933 --> 00:22:02.060
You know, he was about as useful a witness

00:22:02.060 --> 00:22:03.436
as you can imagine.

00:22:03.436 --> 00:22:04.771
But beyond that,

00:22:04.771 --> 00:22:07.398
he was also so far removed

00:22:07.398 --> 00:22:12.195
from the archetypal
greedy financial criminal.

00:22:13.321 --> 00:22:14.155
By this stage,

00:22:14.155 --> 00:22:16.658
he'd been diagnosed with
Asperger's syndrome,

00:22:16.658 --> 00:22:19.160
which kind of provided a useful reason

00:22:19.160 --> 00:22:20.411
for a lot of his actions.

00:22:20.411 --> 00:22:21.246
You know, he's, kind of the way

00:22:21.246 --> 00:22:22.830
that he's treated the authorities.

00:22:23.790 --> 00:22:24.874
So by that stage,

00:22:24.874 --> 00:22:28.795
the U.S. authorities wrote
a note to the judge

00:22:28.795 --> 00:22:30.588
where essentially they said,

00:22:30.588 --> 00:22:33.591
listen, he's had enough punishment.

00:22:33.591 --> 00:22:35.677
He's been incredibly helpful to us.

00:22:35.677 --> 00:22:38.555
We recommend that we let
him off at this point

00:22:38.555 --> 00:22:40.473
with time served.

00:22:40.473 --> 00:22:43.184
And that's quite a remarkable thing

00:22:43.184 --> 00:22:44.852
for the U.S.. government to say.

00:22:45.728 --> 00:22:50.733
And I think if you take
everything into consideration,

00:22:51.150 --> 00:22:55.321
you know, the fact that
he essentially lost

00:22:55.321 --> 00:22:56.823
all of his money,

00:22:56.823 --> 00:23:00.326
you know, I believe that the government

00:23:00.326 --> 00:23:01.536
made the right decision.

00:23:02.537 --> 00:23:04.872
So the judge in the end sentences Nav

00:23:04.872 --> 00:23:07.208
to a year of house arrest.

00:23:08.334 --> 00:23:11.087
You know, there was a great
circularity to the story

00:23:11.087 --> 00:23:13.965
because that's where he got
in trouble in the first place.

00:23:13.965 --> 00:23:17.260
And obviously, as ever,
Nav's timing was impeccable

00:23:17.260 --> 00:23:19.137
because within a couple of months,

00:23:19.137 --> 00:23:20.013
because of the pandemic,

00:23:20.013 --> 00:23:21.639
we were all in lock down anymore.

00:23:33.276 --> 00:23:36.112
I traced Nav's finances very closely.

00:23:36.112 --> 00:23:38.156
And over the course of his trading career

00:23:38.156 --> 00:23:40.617
he made in the region of $70 million.

00:23:42.452 --> 00:23:46.122
I would like to say that the
hidden twist in the story

00:23:46.122 --> 00:23:49.167
is that Nav squirreled away a few million,

00:23:49.167 --> 00:23:51.085
and that, you know, when
this all blows over,

00:23:51.085 --> 00:23:53.379
he'll go to a desert island somewhere

00:23:53.379 --> 00:23:56.466
but sadly, you know, having
looked very closely into it,

00:23:56.466 --> 00:23:57.925
I don't believe that's true.

00:23:57.925 --> 00:23:59.260
Nav is penniless.

00:23:59.260 --> 00:24:00.386
And to be honest with you

00:24:00.386 --> 00:24:03.097
I don't think its made much
difference to his life at all.

00:24:03.097 --> 00:24:05.892
He still cycles around
Hounslow on his bicycle.

00:24:05.892 --> 00:24:08.603
He still plays football
with his mates once a week.

00:24:08.603 --> 00:24:10.938
He still gets a Filet-O-Fish
from McDonald's.

00:24:10.938 --> 00:24:14.067
So for Nav, because the
money never meant anything -

00:24:14.067 --> 00:24:15.777
hasn't changed his life too much.

